OpenFusion licensing overview
=============================

OpenFusion is a modified derivative of FreeCAD. The authoritative license
text for the principal FreeCAD-derived source in this repository is the GNU
Lesser General Public License version 2.1 in the root LICENSE file. Many
source files identify the applicable grant as LGPL-2.1-or-later.

This file is a guide, not a replacement for LICENSE or for the copyright,
SPDX, exception, attribution, and license notices attached to individual
files and components. Some files, assets, submodules, libraries, command-line
programs, fonts, examples, and packaging dependencies use other licenses.
Those terms continue to apply to their respective material.

Before distributing a source or binary build, distributors must:

1. preserve all applicable copyright and license notices;
2. provide the complete corresponding source and build/install scripts
   required by the applicable copyleft licenses;
3. preserve users' ability to modify or replace covered libraries and relink
   where the applicable LGPL terms require it;
4. include the exact third-party notices and license texts for the contents of
   the particular artifact being distributed; and
5. avoid imposing additional terms that conflict with LGPL, GPL, or other
   applicable licenses.

The current third-party notice set is intentionally marked incomplete and is
not release sign-off. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, LICENSES/README.md, and
docs/legal/RELEASE_COMPLIANCE_AUDIT.md.

FreeCAD attribution and historical copyright notices must be retained.
OpenFusion is an independent modified work and must not imply endorsement by
the FreeCAD Project Association, Autodesk, or any other upstream or third
party.
